=begin
  go4invoker.lic -- keeps the invoker's spells up while bigshot hunts AFK.

  The invoker comes to Honeysuckle and Rose Avenue (room 3677) on Four Winds Isle at every
  even hour, game time (US Eastern), and leaves about 15 minutes later. From the logs: she
  thinks "...arriving ... in approximately 15 minutes" at :45, "...currently at Honeysuckle and
  Rose Avenue" at :00, was still answering at :08, and at :15 ASK got "Who are you trying to
  ask?". A spell-up costs 10,000 silver and lasts 4:10, so this goes at every other visit: at
  the last visit before your spells run out, the one where they wouldn't last to her next
  visit two hours later.

  Without bigshot running (resting by hand), a minute before she arrives it goes from wherever
  you are and comes back to that room, unless go2 or a rest chore (eherbs, eloot...) is moving
  you or there's a creature in the room. 11/13 Davu sat in the inn through the 16:00 visit
  because this used to do nothing at all without bigshot.

  charge_me_up_scotty has an orb on the floor where you are, so it's asked to stop first: it
  carries on until it's waiting for mana or between orbs, holds there, and resumes when you're
  back. With it running the trip starts a minute after she's due, so there's no waiting for
  her while the orb shrinks. 11/23 13:59 this walked Picko out between two casts at a new orb:
  the orb was wasted and the charge run ended.

  What a visit looks like with bigshot (all automatic, only when one is due):
    * From 12 minutes before she arrives until 3 minutes after, a hunting bigshot is told to
      rest ($bigshot_should_rest). It finishes the fight, walks home and does its normal
      pre-rest chores. A bigshot that is already resting is simply caught there.
    * Once bigshot is resting in its resting room, it is paused. This waits for its rest
      chores (the profile's resting commands and scripts, and go2) to finish. Then, a minute
      before she arrives:
        - with less than 10,000 silver on hand: go2 bank (the bank nearest the resting room)
          and withdraw what's missing. Bank accounts are per town: on 11/10 Picko's withdraw
          at the Mist Harbor bank failed, so the money has to come from home first;
        - go2 3677 (go2 uses your FWI trinket both ways), wait for her, ASK her twice
          (the first ASK only quotes the price);
        - go2 back to the resting room, restart playsongs if it was playing, unpause bigshot.
    * If something goes wrong (no silver, she never showed, couldn't get there or back), a
      Discord line goes out through deadexit ($deadexit_notice), and bigshot is unpaused
      either way.

  Usage:
    ;go4invoker            watch and go when due (;afk on starts this, ;afk off stops it)
    ;go4invoker bigshot    the same, but only acts while bigshot is running. deadexit starts this
                           one after a login that finds afk_now still on (see afk.lic), because
                           logging out stops the one ;afk on started; ;afk on turns it into the
                           full one. 11/25 Salvi missed the 14:00 visit that way.
    ;go4invoker now        go right now and come back (she must be there or arriving within
                           15 minutes). Pauses bigshot for the trip if it's running.
    ;go4invoker status     last spell-up, next visit, whether that visit is due
    ;go4invoker done       record a spell-up you just got some other way

  While the watcher runs, Lich won't start a second copy, so `status`, `now` and `done` are for
  when it isn't running; `;afk` shows the watcher's status.

  When your spells run out is the later of these two:
    - the last spell-up + 4:10. The time is UserVars.go4invoker_last, set by any "You hand over
      your payment to ... invoker" line seen while this runs (a trip you make by hand too), or by
      eating a spell-up pill while this runs (if it was holding bigshot for a visit, it lets go);
    - your spell timers, when the spells in marker_spells are all up: the shortest one is when
      they run out. A pill lasts exactly as long as the invoker's spells (4:10). This covers a
      pill eaten while this wasn't running (11/24 Salvi ate one at 21:32, and the go4invoker
      started at 21:48 held bigshot for the 22:00 visit, "last spell-up 133h47m ago"), and
      time logged off, because the timers stop while you're out. 11/26 Fizzlestiks paid at
      16:00, was kicked at 17:36 and back at 18:11, so his spells ran until 20:45, not 20:10.
      The old rule (go once the spell-up is 3.5 h old) counted that as a 16:35 spell-up and
      skipped the 20:00 visit, which would have left him without spells from 20:45 to 22:00.

  Needs go2's FWI trinket setting (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>); without one the watcher says so
  and exits. On 11/12 Brayis, Htrowelzzif and Eepo had none set.
=end

module Go4Invoker
  module_function

  INVOKER_ROOM = 3677
  COST         = 10_000
  HOOK         = "go4invoker-hook"

  # Game text, from the saga logs (Salvi 11/11 10:00, Picko 11/10 08:04, Salvi 10/22 10:15).
  PRICE  = /The cost for my services is 10,000 silver/i
  PAID   = /You hand over your payment to .*invoker/i
  POOR   = /You do not have enough for my services/i
  ABSENT = /Who are you trying to ask\?/i
  # Your own pill only: other people's read "Voxy places her dark emerald pill in her mouth".
  PILL   = /You place .*\bpill\b.* in your mouth.*cloud of mana coalesces around you/i
  WITHDRAW_RESULT = /hands you [\d,]+ silvers|already spent what you're trying to withdraw|don't have that much|promissory note|You have no account|insufficient/i

  # Tunables are methods so an edit applies on the next start (constants survive in Lich).
  # Minutes relative to her arrival (0 = she arrives, negative = before).
  def window_open;  -12; end   # start bringing bigshot home / catching it resting
  def force_until;    3; end   # last minute to tell a hunting bigshot to rest
  def leave_at;      -1; end   # leave the resting room for the island
  def leave_at_charging; 1; end # the same, with charge_me_up_scotty running
  def last_leave;    10; end   # too late to start the trip after this
  def give_up_at;    14; end   # stop waiting for her / asking
  def poll_seconds;   5; end
  def go_limit;     180; end   # one go2 run (bank, invoker, home) is stopped after this many seconds

  # How long a spell-up lasts, invoker or pill. Logs: invoker 11/13 Davu, 4:10:00 to the second;
  # pill 9/1 and 10/22 Salvi, the same (10/22 minus 27:47 logged off, when timers stop).
  def spellup_minutes; 250; end

  # Spells both give, that nobody here keeps up as a set by hand. All of them have to be up
  # before the timers count as a spell-up: Foresight and Mindward come from no spell circle of
  # ours. Mantle of Faith and Spirit Shield aren't here because they only last 2 hours.
  def marker_spells; ["Elemental Defense I", "Resist Elements", "Mobility", "Foresight", "Mindward"]; end

  # Scripts that may be running in the resting room but never need waiting for.
  def never_wait_for; %w[playsongs rested timequit go4invoker]; end

  # Without bigshot: scripts that move you or are mid-errand, so the trip waits for them.
  def solo_chores; %w[go2 eherbs ecure eloot unburden buyitems diskwait bounty_chooser undead_bounty ebounty fizzbounty]; end

  def say(msg)
    echo "[go4invoker] #{msg}"
  end

  # deadexit posts it to Discord with "[Name]" in front.
  def notice(text)
    $deadexit_notice = text
  end

  # ---- time -------------------------------------------------------------------

  # US Eastern time (game time) whatever this computer's zone is. DST runs from the second
  # Sunday of March 2:00 to the first Sunday of November 2:00.
  def eastern(t = Time.now)
    utc = t.getutc
    y = utc.year
    mar8 = Time.utc(y, 3, 8)
    dst_start = mar8 + ((7 - mar8.wday) % 7) * 86_400 + 7 * 3600
    nov1 = Time.utc(y, 11, 1)
    dst_end = nov1 + ((7 - nov1.wday) % 7) * 86_400 + 6 * 3600
    utc.getlocal((utc >= dst_start && utc < dst_end ? -4 : -5) * 3600)
  end

  # Minutes from her nearest visit: 0..59.99 after an even-hour arrival, -60..-0.01 before one.
  def rel_minutes(t = Time.now)
    e = eastern(t)
    m = (e.hour % 2) * 60 + e.min + e.sec / 60.0
    m >= 60 ? m - 120 : m
  end

  # Epoch second of the arrival rel_minutes is measured from.
  def visit_epoch(t = Time.now)
    ((t.to_f - rel_minutes(t) * 60) / 60.0).round * 60
  end

  def clock(epoch)
    eastern(Time.at(epoch)).strftime("%H:%M")
  end

  def ago(seconds)
    s = seconds.to_i
    s.negative? ? "just now" : format("%dh%02dm ago", s / 3600, (s % 3600) / 60)
  end

  # ---- the 4-hour clock ---------------------------------------------------------

  # She comes every 2 hours, and the spell-up at a visit lands about a minute after she
  # arrives (she shows at :00:50, payment goes through at :00:51). A visit is due when the
  # spells wouldn't last until her next visit plus this many minutes.
  def end_margin; 5; end

  def last_spellup
    v = UserVars['go4invoker_last']
    v.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? v.to_i : nil
  end

  def record_spellup(at = Time.now.to_i)
    UserVars['go4invoker_last'] = at.to_i
  end

  # When your spells run out (epoch seconds), or nil when there's no spell-up on record and the
  # timers can't be read.
  def spells_end
    last = last_spellup
    [last && last + spellup_minutes * 60, @timers_end].compact.max
  end

  def due_for?(visit)
    e = spells_end
    e.nil? || e < visit + 7200 + end_margin * 60
  end

  # The first visit (this one if it's still on, else the next) that is due.
  def next_due_visit(t = Time.now)
    v = visit_epoch(t)
    v += 7200 if rel_minutes(t) > last_leave
    v += 7200 until due_for?(v)
    v
  end

  def status_line
    last = last_spellup
    e = spells_end
    out = e && e > Time.now.to_i ? "spells run out at #{clock(e)}" : "spells #{e ? "ran out at #{clock(e)}" : 'unknown'}"
    "last spell-up #{last ? "#{ago(Time.now.to_i - last)} (#{clock(last)})" : 'unknown'}; #{out}; " \
      "next trip at the #{clock(next_due_visit)} visit"
  end

  # When the spells you have on now run out, going by their timers (epoch seconds), or nil if
  # any of them isn't up. Read from the game's Active Spells dialog. A timer can be no more than
  # 4:10 from now; anything longer is something else with the same name.
  def timers_end
    now = Time.now.to_f
    ends = marker_spells.map { |name| Effects::Spells.expiration(name).to_f }
    return nil unless ends.all? { |t| t > now }

    [ends.min, now + spellup_minutes * 60].min.to_i
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # Kept rather than looked up each time because the game resends the dialog, and it reads
  # empty for a moment when it does. When the timers outlast the record, says so once, and
  # records a spell-up only if the recorded one's spells would be gone by now even counting
  # nothing logged off: then it's a spell-up this didn't see (a pill while it wasn't running).
  # Otherwise it's time logged off, and the spell-up time on record stays as it was.
  def save_from_timers
    e = timers_end
    return if e.nil?

    before = spells_end
    @timers_end = e
    return if before && e <= before + 60

    last = last_spellup
    now = Time.now.to_i
    if last.nil? || last + spellup_minutes * 60 <= now
      record_spellup(e - spellup_minutes * 60)
      say "your spell timers show a spell-up at #{clock(last_spellup)} (pill or otherwise) -- counting that. #{status_line}."
    else
      say "your spell timers run out at #{clock(e)}, later than the #{clock(last)} spell-up's #{clock(last + spellup_minutes * 60)} " \
          "(timers stop while you're logged off) -- going by the timers. #{status_line}."
    end
  end

  # Everything that can tell us about a spell-up we didn't buy ourselves.
  def update_spellups
    save_paid
    save_from_timers
  end

  # Any spell-up counts, a manual one included. The hook only sets a global; the main loop saves it.
  def install_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK) rescue nil
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK, proc { |line|
      begin
        $go4invoker_paid_at = Time.now.to_i if line =~ PAID || line =~ PILL
      rescue StandardError
        nil
      end
      line
    })
  end

  def remove_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK) rescue nil
  end

  def save_paid
    at = $go4invoker_paid_at
    return unless at

    $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
    record_spellup(at)
  end

  # ---- where things are -----------------------------------------------------------

  def op
    v = UserVars['op']
    v.is_a?(Hash) ? v : {}
  end

  # The running bigshot's own settings ($bigshot is the instance bigshot.lic sets when it
  # starts). They win over UserVars.op, which can change under a running bigshot: on 11/11
  # 23:25 ;huntplan rewrote op (resting room 228) while the bigshot started at 23:20 kept
  # 1259, so at the 11/12 08:00 visit this waited for room 228 and never caught Fizzlestiks.
  def live_bigshot_setting(name)
    bs = $bigshot
    return nil unless bs && bigshot? && bs.respond_to?(name)

    bs.public_send(name)
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # A list setting (resting commands etc.) as an array of strings: live bigshot first, then op.
  def bigshot_list(live_name, op_key)
    v = live_bigshot_setting(live_name)
    v = op[op_key] if v.nil?
    Array(v).join(',').split(',').map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
  end

  def resting_room
    live = live_bigshot_setting(:RESTING_ROOM_ID)
    return live.to_i if live.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ && live.to_i.positive?

    id = op['resting_room_id'].to_s.strip
    id =~ /\A\d+\z/ ? id.to_i : nil
  end

  def room_id
    Room.current&.id
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # go2 only gets to Four Winds with the trinket (every mapped way onto the isle is a
  # trinket teleport). No path search here: one that never finds 3677 walks the whole map.
  def fwi_trinket
    UserVars['mapdb_fwi_trinket'].to_s.strip
  end

  # A live creature on the game's own target list (town folk and the invoker aren't on it).
  def creatures_here?
    Array(GameObj.targets).any?
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def invoker_here?
    (Array(GameObj.npcs) + Array(GameObj.loot)).any? { |o| o.noun.to_s =~ /\Ainvoker\z/i || o.name.to_s =~ /\binvoker\b/i }
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  # go2 with a time limit. go2 restarts itself forever when a step fails (11/15: its FWI
  # `turn` hit the wrong amulet, "You can't turn that.", and it retried every 5 s until the
  # connection dropped nine hours later, with bigshot paused the whole night). A normal run to
  # 3677 or back takes about 20 s, a bank trip a little more; past go_limit it is stopped, and
  # the caller treats the room it is standing in as the result.
  def go(target)
    Script.run_child("go2", "#{target} --disable-confirm", { quiet: true }, timeout: go_limit)
  rescue StandardError => e
    say "!! go2 to #{target} didn't finish in #{go_limit}s (#{e.class}) -- stopped it."
  end

  # The FWI trinket name has to pick out ONE item in the inventory. go2 and eloot look it up
  # with GameObj[name]: a single word matches the first item with that noun, a longer name
  # matches the end of the item's name. Picko's setting was "amulet" while he wears a ruby
  # amulet and a memorial candle amulet, so go2 turned the wrong one. Returns nil when it is
  # fine, otherwise a sentence saying what is wrong.
  def trinket_problem
    name = fwi_trinket
    esc = Regexp.escape(name)
    hits = Array(GameObj.inv).select do |o|
      if name.split(' ').length == 1 then o.noun.to_s == name
      else o.name.to_s == name || o.name.to_s =~ /\b#{esc}\z/i
      end
    end
    return "no worn or carried item matches the FWI trinket #{name.inspect}." if hits.empty?
    return nil if hits.length == 1

    "the FWI trinket #{name.inspect} matches #{hits.length} items (#{hits.map(&:name).join('; ')}) so go2 may turn " \
    "the wrong one. Use a longer name: ;go2 --fwi-trinket=<more of the item's name>"
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # ---- bigshot --------------------------------------------------------------------

  def bigshot?
    Script.running?("bigshot")
  end

  # Waiting in its rest loop, bigshot reads :ready, not :resting: should_hunt? calls
  # group_should_hunt?, which sets :ready for a solo hunter on every pass (bigshot.lic ~866).
  # 11/12 08:00 Fizzlestiks sat in 1259 like that and was never caught.
  def resting_at_home?
    home = resting_room
    !home.nil? && %i[resting ready].include?($bigshot_status) && room_id == home
  end

  # Scripts bigshot runs and waits on around a rest: the profile's "script X" resting and
  # hunting-prep commands, its resting scripts, and go2. Prep is in there because bigshot can
  # turn from resting to gearing up in the instant between the check and the pause.
  def rest_chores
    cmds = bigshot_list(:RESTING_COMMANDS, 'resting_commands') + bigshot_list(:HUNTING_PREP_COMMANDS, 'hunting_prep_commands')
    named = cmds.filter_map { |c| c[/\Ascript\s+(\S+)/i, 1] }
    named += bigshot_list(:RESTING_SCRIPTS, 'resting_scripts').filter_map { |s| s.split(/\s+/).first }
    (named + %w[go2]).uniq(&:downcase).reject { |n| never_wait_for.any? { |x| x.casecmp?(n) } }
  end

  def busy_chores
    rest_chores.select { |n| Script.running?(n) }
  end

  def pause_bigshot
    return false unless bigshot? && !Script.paused?("bigshot")

    Script.pause("bigshot")
    @paused_bigshot = true
  end

  def unpause_bigshot
    return unless @paused_bigshot

    @paused_bigshot = false
    Script.unpause("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot") && Script.paused?("bigshot")
  end

  # ---- music ----------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Stops playsongs (its before_dying stows the instrument) and returns its arguments for the restart.
  def stop_music
    s = Script.running.find { |x| x.name.to_s.casecmp?("playsongs") }
    return nil unless s

    args = s.vars[0].to_s
    Script.kill("playsongs")
    deadline = Time.now + 15
    sleep 0.2 while Script.running?("playsongs") && Time.now < deadline
    args
  end

  def restart_music(args)
    return if args.nil? || Script.running?("playsongs")

    args.strip.empty? ? Script.start("playsongs") : Script.start("playsongs", args)
  end

  # ---- charge_me_up_scotty ----------------------------------------------------------

  def charging?
    Script.running?("charge_me_up_scotty")
  end

  # Ask charge_me_up_scotty to stop, and wait until it has (it sets $charge_me_up_scotty_held)
  # or has finished. $go4invoker_trip stays set until trip is done with it. False if it never
  # got to a stopping place in time to see her.
  def hold_charging
    return true unless charging?

    say "waiting for charge_me_up_scotty to get to a stopping place."
    $go4invoker_trip = true
    while charging? && !$charge_me_up_scotty_held
      return false if rel_minutes >= give_up_at - 1

      sleep 0.5
    end
    # If it ended instead, it may have been on its way somewhere
    until charging? || !Script.running?("go2")
      return false if rel_minutes >= give_up_at - 1

      sleep 0.5
    end
    true
  end

  # ---- the trip -------------------------------------------------------------------

  def silver_on_hand
    Lich::Util.silver_count.to_i
  rescue StandardError
    0
  end

  # Have 10,000 silver in hand, from the bank nearest to where we stand. Returns true/false.
  def ensure_silver
    have = silver_on_hand
    return true if have >= COST

    need = COST - have
    go("bank")
    waitrt?
    line = dothistimeout("withdraw #{need} silver", 6, WITHDRAW_RESULT).to_s
    have = silver_on_hand
    return true if have >= COST

    say "only #{have} silver after the withdraw (the teller said: #{line.strip[0, 120].inspect})."
    false
  end

  # Returns :paid, :poor, :absent or :no_answer.
  def ask_invoker
    2.times do
      waitrt?
      line = dothistimeout("ask invoker for spells", 5, Regexp.union(PRICE, PAID, POOR, ABSENT)).to_s
      if line =~ PAID
        record_spellup
        $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
        return :paid
      end
      return :poor if line =~ POOR
      return :absent if line =~ ABSENT
      return :no_answer unless line =~ PRICE
    end
    :no_answer
  end

  # Standing in 3677: wait for her to show, then ask. Asks blind every 20 s from her arrival time
  # on, in case she doesn't show up in the room objects.
  def get_spells
    next_probe = Time.now
    loop do
      r = rel_minutes
      if invoker_here? || (r >= 0 && Time.now >= next_probe)
        result = ask_invoker
        return result unless result == :absent

        next_probe = Time.now + 20
      end
      return :absent if r >= give_up_at || r < -20

      sleep 1
    end
  end

  # Bank if needed, island, spells, home. Returns :paid, :poor, :no_silver, :absent,
  # :no_answer, :unreachable, :no_trinket or :charging.
  def trip
    if (problem = trinket_problem)
      say "!! not going: #{problem}"
      notice("go4invoker skipped the invoker trip: #{problem}")
      return :no_trinket
    end
    home = nil
    music = nil
    result = nil
    begin
      unless hold_charging
        result = :charging
        return result
      end
      home = room_id
      music = stop_music
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      unless ensure_silver
        result = :no_silver
        return result
      end
      go(INVOKER_ROOM)
      if room_id != INVOKER_ROOM
        go(INVOKER_ROOM) # one retry: go2 sometimes stops after a teleport
      end
      if room_id != INVOKER_ROOM
        result = :unreachable
        return result
      end
      result = get_spells
    ensure
      if home && room_id != home
        go(home)
        go(home) if room_id != home
      end
      back = home.nil? || room_id == home
      say "!! couldn't get back to room #{home} (in #{room_id.inspect})." unless back
      notice("go4invoker could not get back to room #{home} after the invoker trip (now in #{room_id.inspect}).") unless back
      restart_music(music) if back
      $go4invoker_trip = nil # lets charge_me_up_scotty carry on
    end
    result
  end

  def report(result, visit)
    case result
    when :paid
      say "spelled up. #{status_line}."
    when :no_silver
      notice("invoker trip skipped: couldn't get 10,000 silver from the bank (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! couldn't get 10,000 silver -- no spells this visit."
    when :poor
      notice("the invoker said I didn't have enough silver (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! she said you don't have enough silver."
    when :absent
      notice("the invoker never showed at Honeysuckle and Rose Avenue (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! she never showed by #{give_up_at} past the hour."
    when :no_trinket
      nil # trip already said why and sent the notice
    when :charging
      notice("invoker trip skipped: charge_me_up_scotty never got to a stopping place (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! charge_me_up_scotty never got to a stopping place -- no spells this visit."
    when :unreachable
      notice("go4invoker couldn't get to room #{INVOKER_ROOM} (FWI trinket?) for the #{clock(visit)} visit.")
      say "!! couldn't get to room #{INVOKER_ROOM}. Is go2's FWI trinket set (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>)?"
    else
      notice("the invoker didn't answer (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      say "!! no answer from the invoker."
    end
  end

  # A pill (or another spell-up) while bigshot is being held for the visit.
  def spelled_up_meanwhile?(visit)
    update_spellups
    return false if due_for?(visit)

    say "you've been spelled up since -- not going to the invoker. #{status_line}."
    true
  end

  # bigshot is resting at home inside the window: hold it, let the chores finish, go.
  def run_visit(visit)
    pause_bigshot
    say "holding bigshot for the invoker's #{clock(visit)} visit."
    said = false
    until (busy = busy_chores).empty?
      return :spelled_up if spelled_up_meanwhile?(visit)

      if rel_minutes > last_leave
        say "rest chores (#{busy.join(', ')}) still running at #{last_leave} past -- skipping this visit."
        notice("invoker trip skipped: bigshot's rest chores (#{busy.join(', ')}) ran past #{clock(visit + last_leave * 60)}.")
        return :late
      end
      say "waiting for #{busy.join(', ')} to finish." unless said
      said = true
      sleep 1
    end
    while rel_minutes < leave_at
      return :spelled_up if spelled_up_meanwhile?(visit)

      sleep 1
    end
    return :spelled_up if spelled_up_meanwhile?(visit)

    result = trip
    report(result, visit)
    result
  ensure
    unpause_bigshot
  end

  # No bigshot running (resting by hand): go from wherever you are, a minute before she
  # arrives, once nothing is moving you and there's nothing to fight.
  def solo_tick(visit, r)
    return :solo_waiting if r < (charging? ? leave_at_charging : leave_at)

    busy = solo_chores.select { |n| Script.running?(n) }
    why = if busy.any? then "#{busy.join(', ')} running"
          elsif creatures_here? then "a creature in the room"
          end
    if why
      say "waiting to leave for the invoker: #{why}." unless @solo_blocked == visit
      @solo_blocked = visit
      @solo_why = why
      return :solo_blocked
    end

    @handled_visit = visit
    say "bigshot isn't running -- going to the invoker from room #{room_id.inspect}."
    result = trip
    report(result, visit)
    :solo_visited
  end

  # One poll of the watcher. Returns a symbol saying what it did (for tests).
  def tick(now = Time.now)
    update_spellups
    visit = visit_epoch(now)
    r = rel_minutes(now)
    if r > last_leave && @solo_blocked == visit && @handled_visit != visit && due_for?(visit)
      @handled_visit = visit
      say "!! never got to leave for the #{clock(visit)} visit (#{@solo_why})."
      notice("invoker trip skipped: #{@solo_why} until #{last_leave} past (#{clock(visit)} visit).")
      return :solo_skipped
    end
    return :outside if r < window_open || r > last_leave
    return :not_due unless due_for?(visit)
    return :handled if @handled_visit == visit
    return $go4invoker_bigshot_only ? :no_bigshot : solo_tick(visit, r) unless bigshot?
    return :bigshot_paused if Script.paused?("bigshot") # someone else (deader, disarmguard) paused it
    return :no_resting_room if resting_room.nil?

    if resting_at_home?
      @handled_visit = visit
      run_visit(visit)
      return :visited
    end
    return :resting_elsewhere if $bigshot_status == :resting # on its way home
    return :too_late_to_force if r > force_until
    return :forced if @forced_visit == visit

    @forced_visit = visit
    $rest_reason = "invoker spell-up." if $rest_reason.to_s.strip.empty?
    $bigshot_should_rest = true
    say "the invoker arrives at #{clock(visit)} -- sending bigshot home to rest first."
    :force_rest
  end

  def watch
    if fwi_trinket.empty?
      say "go2 has no FWI trinket for #{Char.name}, so it can't get to the invoker on Four Winds Isle. " \
          "Set one with ;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name> and start this again. Exiting."
      return
    end
    save_from_timers
    say "watching#{' (only while bigshot runs)' if $go4invoker_bigshot_only}. #{status_line}."
    loop do
      exit if checkdead
      begin
        tick
      rescue StandardError => e
        say "error: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
        unpause_bigshot
      end
      $go4invoker_status = status_line
      sleep poll_seconds
    end
  end

  def now_command
    if fwi_trinket.empty?
      say "go2 has no FWI trinket for #{Char.name} (;go2 --fwi-trinket=<name>), so it can't get to Four Winds Isle."
      return
    end
    r = rel_minutes
    visit = visit_epoch
    if r >= give_up_at || r < -15
      nxt = visit + (r >= 0 ? 7200 : 0)
      say "she isn't there now; next visit at #{clock(nxt)}."
      return
    end
    pause_bigshot
    begin
      waitrt?
      result = trip
      report(result, visit)
    ensure
      unpause_bigshot
    end
  end

  def run(arg)
    @paused_bigshot = false
    @handled_visit = nil
    @forced_visit = nil
    @solo_blocked = nil
    @solo_why = nil
    @timers_end = nil
    $go4invoker_paid_at = nil
    $go4invoker_trip = nil
    arg = arg.to_s.strip.downcase
    $go4invoker_bigshot_only = arg == "bigshot"
    case arg
    when "", "bigshot"
      install_hook
      watch
    when "now"
      install_hook
      now_command
      save_paid
    when "status"
      save_from_timers
      say status_line
      say "bigshot #{bigshot? ? 'running' : 'not running'}; resting room #{resting_room.inspect}; " \
          "FWI trinket #{UserVars['mapdb_fwi_trinket'].inspect}"
    when "done"
      record_spellup
      say "recorded a spell-up now. #{status_line}."
    else
      say "Unknown option '#{arg}'. Use ;go4invoker, ;go4invoker bigshot, ;go4invoker now, ;go4invoker status or ;go4invoker done."
    end
  end
end

before_dying do
  Go4Invoker.unpause_bigshot
  Go4Invoker.remove_hook
  Go4Invoker.save_paid
  $go4invoker_trip = nil
  $go4invoker_status = nil
  $go4invoker_bigshot_only = nil
end

Go4Invoker.run(Script.current.vars[1])
